Cause and design

The sidebar rendered the backend payload correctly; the backend published CPU with zero values when its single startup probe was unavailable. GPU memory refresh was coupled to Ollama startup and never retried. On macOS, real CEF startup proved that sysctl/vm_stat stdout pipes can remain open during the initial process burst. The fix makes memory observation an independently supervised 10-second loop, retains the last successful bounded snapshot, and uses sysinfo directly for Apple unified memory. Linux and Windows keep dedicated-VRAM probes, with controlled sysfs parsing and a restored Windows performance-counter fallback. GpuMemoryKind is now the shared authority for forecast and sidebar behavior.

User-visible contract

Apple Silicon reports RAM. Linux and Windows report VRAM. CPU is shown only when Ollama reports a loaded model with zero GPU allocation. An idle unavailable probe hides the badge instead of displaying CPU with missing values. Existing settings text was updated in all seven locales.

